==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈdʒəʊ.vi.ən/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈdʒoʊ.vi.ən/}}
* {{hyphenation|en|Jov|i|an}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dyew-}}
From {{der|en|la|Iovis}}, genitive of {{m|la|Iuppiter}}, analysable as {{suffix|en|Jove|ian}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|astronomy}} Pertaining to the [[planet]] [[Jupiter]].
#: {{synonyms|en|Jovial}}
# {{lb|en|Roman mythology}} Pertaining to the [[Roman#Adjective|Roman]] [[god]] [[Jove]] or Jupiter (the [[counterpart]] of the [[Greek#Adjective|Greek]] god [[Zeus]]); Jove-like; [[befit]]ting Jupiter.
#: {{synonyms|en|Jovial}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1926|author=Sir Arthur Conan Doyle|authorlink=Arthur Conan Doyle|title=The Land of Mist|url=http://gutenberg.net.au/ebooks06/0601351h.html|passage=He did not admit of equals. But as a patron he was superb. With his '''Jovian''' air, his colossal condescension, his amused smile, his general suggestion of the god descending to the mortal, he could be quite overpowering in his amiability.}}

